# gh-391: Parity: ADO WIQL link queries (workItemRelations) + agents #875/#876 on the Dart runtime

## Description

Two things came out of IstiN/dmtools-agents#870/#871 (ADO question subtasks). The Java side is merged (epam/dm.ai#700).

**1. WIQL link queries.** Dart `AdoClient.listWorkItems` does `wiqlStubIds(decoded['workItems'])`, the same blind spot Java had: a `FROM WorkItemLinks` query answers with `workItemRelations` (flat queries use `workItems`), so it returns nothing. Mirror Java's `extractWorkItemIds`: flat ids in order; for relations take the **target** of every link, skip the anchoring source row (no `rel`), drop duplicates. Same tests: flat order, link targets + anchor skipped, duplicates / empty / missing-target shapes, and a search over a link query that fetches the child.

**2. Agents changes that need the Dart runtime checked (no Dart code expected):** dmtools-agents #875 (content output writes through the configured tracker; `assignForReview` skips only the assignment when there is no initiator) and #876 (ADO question subtasks created via `createTicketWithParent`, WIQL `jira.questions.fetchJql` executed on ADO). After the next agents bump, run the agents suite on the Dart runtime. `createTicketWithParent` on ADO in Dart must: create the work item, link it with relationship `parent`, add the label, and `ado_set_priority` must exist (it is called non-fatally).
----
{
  "key": "gh-391",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "Parity: ADO WIQL link queries (workItemRelations) + agents #875/#876 on the Dart runtime",
    "description": "Two things came out of IstiN/dmtools-agents#870/#871 (ADO question subtasks). The Java side is merged (epam/dm.ai#700).\n\n**1. WIQL link queries.** Dart `AdoClient.listWorkItems` does `wiqlStubIds(decoded['workItems'])`, the same blind spot Java had: a `FROM WorkItemLinks` query answers with `workItemRelations` (flat queries use `workItems`), so it returns nothing. Mirror Java's `extractWorkItemIds`: flat ids in order; for relations take the **target** of every link, skip the anchoring source row (no `rel`), drop duplicates. Same tests: flat order, link targets + anchor skipped, duplicates / empty / missing-target shapes, and a search over a link query that fetches the child.\n\n**2. Agents changes that need the Dart runtime checked (no Dart code expected):** dmtools-agents #875 (content output writes through the configured tracker; `assignForReview` skips only the assignment when there is no initiator) and #876 (ADO question subtasks created via `createTicketWithParent`, WIQL `jira.questions.fetchJql` executed on ADO). After the next agents bump, run the agents suite on the Dart runtime. `createTicketWithParent` on ADO in Dart must: create the work item, link it with relationship `parent`, add the label, and `ado_set_priority` must exist (it is called non-fatally)."
  }
}

